+# aims Guide State
+
+## Mode
+
+auto
+
+## Loop cursor
+
+ready-to-choose-next
+
+## Current objective
+
+**Kind:** add-feature
+
+**Objective:** One owner for "which timeout does this send use" — the transport adapter — so a default set
+once on the adapter a Session mounts governs every send through it (request(), send(), each redirect hop)
+unless the call supplies its own; Session gains no timeout state (standing Decision kept, PO reconfirmed).
+
+**Why now:** PO wants a set-once default so a forgotten `timeout=` cannot hang forever; PO ruled that the
+default belongs to the adapter, not the Session.
+
+**Exit criteria:**
+- [x] Adapter built with a default, mounted on a Session; `s.get(url)` with no timeout -> the default reaches urllib3.
+- [x] Call-level timeout (float, tuple, urllib3 Timeout) wins wholly over the default (no per-component merge).
+- [x] Explicit `timeout=None` on a call == omitted (requests' None-means-unset grain; adapter cannot tell them apart);
+      explicit "wait forever" stays expressible via `(None, None)` / `Timeout(connect=None, read=None)` and bypasses the default.
+- [x] `Session.send(prepared)` directly and every redirect hop use the default (falsifier: a hop sent with no timeout).
+- [x] Adapter without a default: resolved timeout is bit-for-bit today's (None -> no timeout).
+- [x] Invalid default ((1,2,3), "foo", negative) rejected at adapter construction, not at first send.
+- [x] Adapter with a default survives pickling (alone and inside a pickled Session); an adapter state pickled
+      before this change unpickles to "no default".
+- [x] `add_headers` hook sees the effective timeout.
+- [x] Session has no `timeout` attribute / `__attrs__` entry; sessions.py logic untouched.
+
+**Preserve:**
+- All tests except the 4 known-environmental TestTimeout connect-timeout failures, unedited.
+- Per-call timeout behaviour and ValueError messages for invalid per-call timeouts.
+
+**Do not optimize for:**
+- A Session-level convenience (ruled out by the standing Decision).
+- Per-component merging of call tuple with default; module-level `requests.get` defaults.
+
+## Worker handoff (drafted — do not execute before the build command)
+
+ROLE: implementation Worker (executed as a separate phase — no subagent facility in this host).
+DESIGN GOAL: timeout resolution has one owner in HTTPAdapter; a construction-time default participates in it.
+BEHAVIOR: the exit criteria above. PRESERVE/NON-GOALS: above. Match adapters.py's grain (max_retries is
+normalised at construction; pickled via __attrs__). Test-first; every decision tested.
+RETURN: code + tests + design reasoning; result met|partially_met|invalidated|blocked.
+
+## Open assumptions (unproven — carried, not filed)
+
+- none
+
+## Open Guide TODO
+
+- [x] PO decision: keep the Decision; default lives on the transport adapter.
+- [x] Explicit per-call `timeout=None`: resolved from repository grain (None = unset, as merge_setting does
+      for verify/stream/cert; an adapter receives identical None either way) — explicit "forever" = (None, None).
+      Flag to PO in the summary.
+- [x] File the adapter decision in src/requests/adapters.py.md; note in sessions.py.md that its caveat
+      ("HTTPAdapter stores no default timeout") no longer holds.
+
+## Last evaluated result
+
+met (add-feature). Guide-measured: full suite 646 passed, only the 4 known environmental TestTimeout
+failures; 32 new tests in tests/test_adapters.py cover every exit criterion (default reaches urllib3 via
+request(), send(), each redirect hop; call wins wholly; explicit None == omitted; (None, None) waits forever;
+invalid default fails at construction; pickling incl. legacy state; add_headers sees effective timeout;
+Session has no timeout state; module-level calls unchanged). sessions.py untouched. Review finding fixed in
+loop: subclass skipping HTTPAdapter.__init__ would have raised AttributeError -> class-level default.
