 - \[Short description of non-trivial change.\]
 
+**Improvements**
+
+- `HTTPAdapter` accepts a default `timeout`, applied to every request sent
+  through it that does not pass its own. Mount one on a `Session` to give all
+  of the session's requests a default timeout. `Session` itself still holds no
+  timeout.
+
 
 2.34.2 (2026-05-14)
 -------------------
diff --git a/docs/user/advanced.rst b/docs/user/advanced.rst
index f5209a5..124a5bc 100644
--- a/docs/user/advanced.rst
+++ b/docs/user/advanced.rst
@@ -1120,6 +1120,24 @@ coffee.
 
     r = requests.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)
 
+To give every request made through a :class:`Session <requests.Session>` a
+default timeout, set it on the transport adapter the session sends through,
+once, instead of repeating ``timeout=`` on each call::
+
+    s = requests.Session()
+    adapter = requests.adapters.HTTPAdapter(timeout=(3.05, 27))
+    s.mount('http://', adapter)
+    s.mount('https://', adapter)
+
+    s.get('https://github.com')              # uses (3.05, 27)
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=60)  # its own timeout replaces the default
+
+A request whose timeout is ``None``, or not given, uses the adapter's default;
+with a default in place, pass ``(None, None)`` to wait forever on one request.
+The default lives on the adapter rather than on the session because a timeout
+is connection behaviour, which adapters own. Mount the adapter on every prefix
+whose requests should use it.
+
 .. note:: The connect timeout applies to each connection attempt to an IP address.
           If multiple addresses exist for a domain name, the underlying ``urllib3`` will
           try each address sequentially until one successfully connects.
